<http://data.silknow.org/object/a24c0e21-76eb-3710-80e5-df647c23709b/observation/4>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/historical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The coat of arms might be connected to the Florentine family, la famiglia aretina dei Bacci.\n\nA brisé fan with narrower but similarly-shaped sticks features in a portrait of a ‘Venetian Courtesan’ by Girolamo Forabosco (c.1605-1679) in the Uffizi Gallery.\n\nA similar fan also features in a portrait of Elizabeth Stuart, Queen of Bohemia, by Robert Peake the Younger, 1603, in the Greenwich Maritime Museum."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/a24c0e21-76eb-3710-80e5-df647c23709b> .

